1
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:32,900


2
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,980
It appears you're out of options, Pharaoh.

3
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:07,297
Thanks to my nightmare
Steelcade, you can't attack.

4
00:01:07,380 --> 00:01:11,757
And in one more turn, you'll be finished
and your Millennium Puzzle will be mine.

5
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:12,670
Never!

6
00:01:12,753 --> 00:01:14,757
As long as I believe in
the heart of the cards,

7
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:17,280
you won't succeed in claiming my puzzle.

8
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:20,557
Your misguided faith is
completely pathetic when compared

9
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:23,537
to the overwhelming power
of my Egyptian God card.

10
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:26,738
But you'll see that first
hand in just one more turn,

11
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:29,737
when my breeding machine
produces the third slime token,

12
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:32,114
giving me enough monsters to sacrifice.

13
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:34,500
Then I'll summon my great beast,

14
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:38,340
an ancient creature of unbeatable
strength to destroy you.

15
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,380
All systems go.

16
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:44,137
Commence download of
real-time satellite imaging.

17
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:45,050
Check.

18
00:01:45,133 --> 00:01:47,879
Confirm system data link
with all active dual disks.

19
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:48,890
Check.

20
00:01:48,973 --> 00:01:53,324
Resume digital scan of Battle City Tournament
gameplay and card tracking software.

21
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:56,400
Progress report. Ah, Mr. Kaiba.

22
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:59,057
Has my satellite tracking
system recorded any

23
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:01,728
use of the two remaining
Egyptian god cards?

24
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:02,950
No, sir.

25
00:02:03,033 --> 00:02:05,115
But we are searching around the clock.

26
00:02:05,260 --> 00:02:08,260
I trust even you won't
screw up this assignment.

27
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:13,326
I've done all the real work programming
my satellite to track every card played.

28
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:17,980
Contact me immediately if an
Egyptian god card appears. Yes, sir.

29
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:22,020
I'm surprised those cards
haven't surfaced yet. Me too.

30
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:26,065
But if they had, our satellite
system would have picked them up.

31
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:31,140
Well then, maybe it's time for me
to go out and find them on my own.

32
00:02:31,340 --> 00:02:34,260
My patience is growing thin. Relax.

33
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:36,877
With all these rare hunters
running around the city,

34
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:40,313
I bet those Egyptian god cards
are right under our noses.

35
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:45,069
And once I have all three, I'll have
the most powerful deck in duel monsters.

36
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:50,760
I'll be unbeatable, and once again I'll
be known as the world's greatest duelist.

37
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:52,340
Let's go, Mokuba.

38
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:56,720
Wait up, Seto!

39
00:02:58,340 --> 00:03:00,600
History may be on your side, Pharaoh,

40
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:04,760
but destiny is on mine as I draw
closer to winning your puzzle.

41
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:09,868
And once I possess it, only the final
Egyptian god card will be left to claim.

42
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:12,900
When I do, then I'll be the Pharaoh.

43
00:03:13,420 --> 00:03:19,217
You're not worthy of the powers that lie
hidden within you, so I'll take them!

44
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:23,677
For as long as I can remember, I was
taught to obey the ancient scriptures.

45
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:26,940
And to help my family
protect the pharaohs, too.

46
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:32,737
Now I realize that your time as pharaoh
has expired, and I must take your place.

47
00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:35,720
And your puzzle is the key to your power.

48
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:39,925
I wish that I knew more about
what happened in the ancient past.

49
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:43,540
But for now, I know that
I can't let Merrick win.

50
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:44,800
You can't attack.

51
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:46,340
I'll end my turn.

52
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:50,741
That's good, because your
time has run out anyway.

53
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:55,460
Greening machine, create the
third and final slime token.

54
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:58,900
This can't be. He's succeeded.

55
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:02,238
Now I have enough monsters
for my ultimate sacrifice.

56
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:08,140
Finally, the time has come.

57
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:11,460
The sky shall be shrouded in darkness.

58
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:19,840
Prepare to experience an
ancient force like no other!

59
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:28,620
As I sacrifice Jambeater
and my three slime tokens

60
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:34,880
in order to summon the beast
of your ultimate destruction!

61
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:42,540
A creature whose power
is absolutely limitless!

62
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:51,500
Meet your maker, Pharaoh!

63
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:55,460
The last monster you'll ever see!

64
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:59,140
The Egyptian god Slifer the Sky Dragon!

65
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:08,260
You're finished, Yugi!

66
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:10,320
Prepare to feel his wrath!

67
00:05:10,660 --> 00:05:11,740
How can I stop it?

68
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:20,460
You're staring into the
face of defeat, Pharaoh.

69
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:25,272
Slifer the Sky Dragon is one of the
three most feared creatures in history.

70
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:27,200
The Egyptian god monsters.

71
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,140
They cannot be defeated.

72
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:33,080
Every monster has a weakness,
Merrick, and I'll find yours.

73
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:35,637
You're in no position to make threats.

74
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:39,177
You're trapped in my nightmare
steel cage with no way to attack.

75
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:41,057
And you're face to face with an Egyptian

76
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:43,797
god monster whose attack
power is limitless.

77
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:46,560
All you can do is watch it grow stronger.

78
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:48,190
Stronger?

79
00:05:48,273 --> 00:05:49,103
But how?

80
00:05:49,186 --> 00:05:51,760
Allow me to explain how Slifer works.

81
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:57,100
The number of cards I hold in my hand
determines what Slifer's attack power will be.

82
00:05:57,260 --> 00:06:00,457
And since I hold two cards,
it has 2,000 attack points.

83
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:03,481
I'm afraid Slifer is still
weaker than my monster.

84
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:05,560
But this is just the beginning.

85
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:10,400
All thanks to my magic card,
I activate Pot of Green.

86
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:14,717
This card allows me to draw two new cards.

87
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:15,860
Greed is good.

88
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:19,337
I lost one card but gained two,

89
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:24,040
giving me a total of three cards and
Slifer a total of 3,000 attack points.

90
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:28,677
But in Duel Monsters, there's a limit
to how many cards a player can hold.

91
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:31,878
So Slifer the Sky Dragon
has a limit to its strength.

92
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:36,397
Foolish Pharaoh, don't you realize
that every rule is made to be broken?

93
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:40,577
He has no understanding of the
destructive force of an Egyptian god

94
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:45,300
monster because he has no memory of the
days when they devastated the Earth.

95
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:49,437
But he'll learn about Slifer's
power the hard way since I

96
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:53,049
have just the cards to give my
sky dragon infinite strength.

97
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:56,997
I'm afraid any hopes you have
of survival are completely

98
00:06:57,080 --> 00:07:00,720
in vain for no one has ever
defeated an Egyptian god card.

99
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,977
Until now, you're our home.

100
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:06,884
Sniper will wipe you out
with one single attack.

101
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:11,097
Then I'll take your puzzle and send
you to a place of eternal darkness.

102
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,560
The Shadow Realm!

103
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:15,420
Now, prepare to lose.

104
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:20,254
I gotta figure out a way to
bring down Merrick's dragon.

105
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:24,497
My Buster Blader receives 500 attack
points for every dragon on the field.

106
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:28,020
So right now, my monster is
stronger than his Sky Dragon.

107
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:29,960
With 3,100 attack points,

108
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:34,199
my swordsman would slay Merrick's
dragon with one swipe of his lance.

109
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:37,677
But as long as I'm in this cage,

110
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:42,113
I can't attack And by the time I can
attack, his monster may be too strong

111
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:48,620
You see, my Sky Dragon will only
get stronger as I draw more cards

112
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:51,980
So when I draw on my next turn,

113
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:56,297
Slifer will have 4,000 attack points
More than enough to annihilate

114
00:07:56,380 --> 00:08:01,240
your Buster Blader and seriously damage
your life points Then soon enough,

115
00:08:01,420 --> 00:08:02,773
you'll be out of my way

116
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:09,800
Your reign is over, Yami Hand over
that puzzle and accept the inevitable

117
00:08:12,140 --> 00:08:12,970
Never!

118
00:08:13,053 --> 00:08:14,160
I'll trust my deck

119
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:17,977
This card may be able to help,

120
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:21,717
but I'm still trapped for one more
turn If I can hang on until then,

121
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:25,037
maybe I can turn this duel
around I just have to trust

122
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:27,897
the heart of the cards
This duel is far from over,

123
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:29,320
Merrick How sad!

124
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:30,580
You're finished!

125
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:35,100
Just embrace it You've had
your chance to be fair, Oyami.

126
00:08:35,340 --> 00:08:38,520
Now it's time for me to take
over and rule the world.

127
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:41,457
Not if I can help it, Merrick.

128
00:08:41,540 --> 00:08:43,187
It's my destiny to stop you.

129
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:45,920
I'll place these two cards face down.

130
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:49,400
And I summon Koribo in defense mode.

131
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:53,140
Make your move, Merrick.

132
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:55,200
Yes, the moment has now arrived.

133
00:08:57,400 --> 00:09:00,440
Prepare to feel the wrath
of an Egyptian god card.

134
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:06,320
The steel cage is evaporating, leaving
you wide open for annihilation!

135
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:09,277
You are about to witness
an ancient force so

136
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:12,260
mighty it almost destroyed
the entire world!

137
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:19,040
You are powerless against Slifer!

138
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:22,060
Let's end this! I draw,

139
00:09:22,320 --> 00:09:26,117
and since Slifer gets 1,000 attack
points for every card in my hand,

140
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:31,140
Now it's up to 4,000, enough to
incinerate your buster flader.

141
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:36,200
And now, my Egyptian god monster, attack!

142
00:09:41,020 --> 00:09:43,240
You've activated my trap card.

143
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,380
Trap card?

144
00:09:44,580 --> 00:09:46,240
My light force sword.

145
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:49,057
This trap card allows me to slash one card

146
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:51,846
out of your hand for the
duration of the turn.

147
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:53,290
No!

148
00:09:53,373 --> 00:09:57,240
which lowers your dragon's
attack points back to 3,000,

149
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:59,381
making it weaker than my monster.

150
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:04,400
Now, Buster Blader, swing your
mighty sword and slay his dragon!

151
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:09,400
Your Egyptian god card is defeated.

152
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:14,300
Not exactly.

153
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:17,937
You forgot my jam
defender is still in play,

154
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:21,560
which means my revival jam will
intercept all your attacks.

155
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:27,340
And from now on, this magic
card will also be in play.

156
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:29,340
Card of Safe Return!

157
00:10:29,820 --> 00:10:31,100
Card of Safe Return?

158
00:10:31,740 --> 00:10:32,570
Yes,

159
00:10:32,653 --> 00:10:35,297
this rare magic card
lets me draw three new

160
00:10:35,380 --> 00:10:38,620
cards every time my gem
defender reforms itself.

161
00:10:39,060 --> 00:10:41,648
This brings the cards
in my hand up to five,

162
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:46,360
giving Slifer the Sky Dragon a grand
total of 5,000 attack points so far.

163
00:10:47,420 --> 00:10:49,760
5,000 points? Now what?

164
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:55,437
You should have challenged him.

165
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:57,677
You would have destroyed
him one, two, three.

166
00:10:57,760 --> 00:10:58,590
Come on.

167
00:10:58,673 --> 00:11:01,117
You're just two locator
cards away from the finals.

168
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:03,100
He was a lightweight. Huh?

169
00:11:03,380 --> 00:11:05,700
I got a reputation to uphold over here.

170
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:08,457
I can't go dueling every
inexperienced chump I see.

171
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:09,370
What?

172
00:11:09,453 --> 00:11:10,697
You're out of your mind, Joey.

173
00:11:10,780 --> 00:11:13,697
Dude, I don't care if that guy
couldn't even play Go Fish.

174
00:11:13,780 --> 00:11:17,977
His locator cards are just as good as
anyone else's, and you need them now.

175
00:11:18,060 --> 00:11:20,717
Look, Tristan, you don't
understand how it feels.

176
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:23,057
I came in second place in Duelist Kingdom.

177
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:26,677
That puts a lot of pressure on me to kick
some serious geester in this tournament.

178
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:30,113
No one's going to claim Joey
Wheeler did it the easy way.

179
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:33,177
Plus, after the way I've
been dueling lately,

180
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:35,637
I know I'm ready to take
on anyone in Battle City.

181
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:37,300
And I mean anyone! Well,

182
00:11:37,540 --> 00:11:40,677
it's true your dueling skills
have improved quite a bit,

183
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:43,180
especially during your last two duels.

184
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:46,420
But besides having
confidence in oneself, Joey,

185
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:50,417
being a great duelist means knowing
that there's always more to learn.

186
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:52,540
Well, what do we have here?

187
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:55,290
Kaiba?

188
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:59,674
Why is a complete amateur like you
wearing one of my dual discs, Wheeler?

189
00:12:00,180 --> 00:12:01,010
Amateur?

190
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:02,820
I'm going to the top.

191
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:06,186
Looks like someone screwed
up at registration.

192
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:09,280
I'll deal with you later. Come on, Mokuba.

193
00:12:10,180 --> 00:12:12,260
We've wasted enough time here.

194
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:15,900
Tristan, I think I feel a
challenge coming on here.

195
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,957
Maybe you should save
Kaiba for the finals, Joey.

196
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:20,880
Kaiba, you want a piece of me?

197
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:25,330
Joey?

198
00:12:25,413 --> 00:12:27,124
You might want to rethink this.

199
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:31,740
Nobody disses me in front of my friends.

200
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:34,356
Joey, you're an okay duelist and all,

201
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:37,917
but playing against you would be a
complete waste of my big brother's time.

202
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:38,937
This won't take long.

203
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:39,850
Huh?

204
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:45,160
Let's rock and roll. You fool.

205
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:49,800
Looks like I'll have to teach you to
behave, just like the dog you are.

206
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:57,620
Kaiba, you're toast.

207
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:01,340
What's with all this wind, huh?

208
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:04,060
It's a twister.

209
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,860
Your chopper. Mr.

210
00:13:09,020 --> 00:13:12,785
Kaiba, an Egyptian god card was
played exactly five minutes ago.

211
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:14,560
We'll fly you to it.

212
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:17,700
Quit stalling.

213
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,468
There's dueling to be done.

214
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:22,660
It's your lucky day.

215
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:24,870
Huh? What?

216
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:25,880
Later, Joey.

217
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:28,629
We've got a date with
an Egyptian God card.

218
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:30,880
Then it's your lucky day, punk.

219
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:33,453
I was about to wipe the street with you.

220
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:35,640
You better run from me. Whew.

221
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:41,260
Man, did you see the way he took off?

222
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:42,617
You can drop the act.

223
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:44,520
You're safe, Joey. What?

224
00:13:44,760 --> 00:13:46,231
I would have crushed him.

225
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:52,560
More information has just come in.

226
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:57,960
The Egyptian God card was activated
in a duel involving Yu-Gi-Moto.

227
00:13:58,780 --> 00:14:01,940
Yu-Gi, I have a plan, Mokuba.

228
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:04,240
That card will be mine.

229
00:14:05,900 --> 00:14:10,580
And now, Slifer the Sky Dragon,
destroy his Buster Blader!

230
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:15,680
And take a bite out of his life points!

231
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,920
Do you surrender yet?

232
00:14:21,140 --> 00:14:21,970
You're finished!

233
00:14:22,053 --> 00:14:24,080
Slifer will only get stronger,

234
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:28,260
and thanks to my jam defender,
you still can't attack Pharaoh.

235
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:33,111
For if you do, I'll draw more cards and
Slifer will grow even more powerful.

236
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:36,580
Don't you realize there's
no way you can win?

237
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:39,420
Hand over your puzzle!

238
00:14:39,980 --> 00:14:45,420
Once my Egyptian God card finishes you
off, your days as Pharaoh will be over!

239
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:49,637
None of my monsters are strong
enough to beat a Sky Dragon,

240
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,897
so I'm gonna need the
right magic card to do it.

241
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:54,520
Come on, Heart of the Cards. Guide me.

242
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:58,180
Here I go. Now!

243
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:01,780
Magic Cylinder.

244
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:03,397
This card could do the trick,

245
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:06,037
but it has to be combined
with a Magician card to work.

246
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:09,649
And I'm in luck, because I'm
holding the Dark Magician Girl.

247
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:10,890
Perfect!

248
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:13,130
All right.

249
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:15,340
I sacrifice Coribo

250
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:20,160
to summon Dark Magician
Girl in defense mode.

251
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:25,320
By summoning a new monster to the field,

252
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:28,280
you've activated my
dragon's special ability!

253
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:29,620
Oh, no!

254
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:34,500
Its second mouth!

255
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:37,660
Sniper is full of surprises!

256
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:40,000
Even if it's your turn,

257
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:42,177
Sniper will automatically attack every

258
00:15:42,260 --> 00:15:45,025
monster you summon with
its second set of jaws,

259
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:49,237
wiping out 2,000 points from
whichever mode your monster is in.

260
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:53,740
So say goodbye to your
Dark Magician Girl! Oh no!

261
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,860
She only has 1,700 defense points!

262
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:58,440
Sliver, attack!

263
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:04,740
It's time for me to save
my Dark Magician Girl!

264
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:07,480
It's too late! Observe!

265
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:10,260
Why don't you observe?

266
00:16:12,820 --> 00:16:16,660
It really is a pity that your
Magician had to leave us so soon!

267
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:18,560
Who said she's gone?

268
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:20,150
I did.

269
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:21,520
Guess again.

270
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:23,995
I activated Magical Hats just in time.

271
00:16:24,440 --> 00:16:27,000
So she's hiding inside one of those hats?

272
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:28,181
Not just hiding.

273
00:16:28,380 --> 00:16:31,340
She's inside preparing to
launch a counterattack.

274
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:35,680
Yugi, your monster's not strong
enough not to defeat Slifer.

275
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:40,540
It's true that your dragon
is powerful, Merrick.

276
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:41,920
But I have faith.

277
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:48,080
And so I place two cards face
down beneath my Magical Hats.

278
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:53,840
Your hats merely provide you with a
temporary hiding place And in the meantime,

279
00:16:54,340 --> 00:16:55,170
Pharaoh

280
00:16:55,540 --> 00:16:58,917
I'll play my own magic card And it will

281
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:02,940
make my dragon's power infinite You see,

282
00:17:03,280 --> 00:17:06,297
infinite cards let me
exceed the six-card limit

283
00:17:06,380 --> 00:17:10,160
And hold as many cards
as I wish in my hand No,

284
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:11,220
that can't be

285
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:16,137
Since Slifer gets 1,000
attack points for every card

286
00:17:16,220 --> 00:17:20,120
in my hand Now there's no
limit to my monster's power.

287
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:25,340
Slifer, unleash your thunder
force on the right hand's hat.

288
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:30,140
You made a lucky guess, Merrick.

289
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:33,260
You couldn't hide her forever.

290
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:37,680
This duel's not over.

291
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:43,420
It may as well be your
monster is destroyed.

292
00:17:43,940 --> 00:17:44,780
What's this?

293
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:49,600
She's absorbing my attack!

294
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:51,234
That's right, Merrick.

295
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:55,900
It seems you have forgotten I also
hid two trap cards under that hat.

296
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:59,760
Magic Cylinder and my Spellbinding Circle!

297
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:03,617
So I'll weaken your Sky
Dragon's power and then

298
00:18:03,700 --> 00:18:07,360
redirect his own Thunder Force
attack right back at him! Fire!

299
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:10,640
Say goodbye, Merrick.

300
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,150
Never!

301
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:15,820
You can't attack me with
my Revival Jam in play!

302
00:18:18,860 --> 00:18:22,360
So your plasma monster can
even block redirected attacks?

303
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:26,620
That's exactly right, Barrow.

304
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:32,000
Then it regenerates unharmed, which
also means I can draw three new cards.

305
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:35,460
So my Sky Dragon grows even stronger!

306
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:40,320
Plus, I'll draw again, giving it a
total of over 8,000 attack points!

307
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:43,817
That Egyptian god is
unstoppable! Precisely!

308
00:18:43,900 --> 00:18:46,959
And since your Spellbinding
Circle card has expired,

309
00:18:47,180 --> 00:18:50,356
Slyper gains back more attack
points, giving it 9,000.

310
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:53,420
Now, Slyper, demolish
his Dark Magician Girl!

311
00:19:02,320 --> 00:19:08,197
Behold, the ultimate five-card combination
that makes me completely indestructible.

312
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:11,420
When these five almighty
cards are played together,

313
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:14,562
they complete a strategy
that cannot be defeated.

314
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:18,617
My Egyptian god card will
continue to grow stronger,

315
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:21,520
and your attacks are completely useless.

316
00:19:22,040 --> 00:19:23,080
Oh, no.

317
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:27,080
I can't let Merrick win my puzzle.

318
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:30,620
Get on your feet, Yugi.

319
00:19:31,560 --> 00:19:32,390
Kaiba!

320
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:36,840
Since when do you bow to your rivals?

321
00:19:37,420 --> 00:19:38,250
Never.

322
00:19:38,333 --> 00:19:42,417
Then get up and stop embarrassing
yourself So you can defeat

323
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:47,700
this nobody And relieve him of his
Egyptian God card And do it now

324
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:51,957
Don't let this punk win
You can take down Slifer

325
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:56,560
the Sky Dragon Just find
out its weakness Unless,

326
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:58,741
of course, you've lost your touch

327
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:03,837
If you still have what it takes
Then get up and prove it to me

328
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:08,740
now Once I learn its weakness I'll
take Slifer from Yugi And soon,

329
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:11,620
I'll have the most
powerful deck in the world!
